     "title": "A Readiness Check Before You Install Leader-Leader",
     "content": "Before importing Leader-Leader mechanisms wholesale, a leader can run a structured readiness check across the three limits this lesson has raised.\n\nFirst, map your decisions by coupling and reversibility, as the previous cards described, and be explicit and public about which category each falls into -- a team that knows exactly which decisions carry pushed-down authority and which remain centralized will not experience the ambiguity that causes both failure modes above.\n\nSecond, honestly assess whether the competence-building infrastructure exists before extending authority. Ask: is there a real, peer-verified qualification pathway (see Lesson 10) that people actually pass through, or is 'empowerment' being announced onto a workforce that has not yet had the chance to build the judgment it requires? If the answer is the latter, the correct sequence is to build the qualification and mentorship system first, and delay the authority delegation until competence is demonstrably in place -- exactly the order Marquet followed on Santa Fe, where competence-building preceded and enabled control delegation, not the reverse.\n\nThird, treat the book itself with appropriate epistemic humility. It is an compelling, well-told single case study, useful for generating hypotheses and vivid mental models, but it is not a controlled study, and Santa Fe had resources (rigorous selection, extensive training pipelines, redundant safety systems) that most civilian organizations cannot replicate. Before generalizing a specific mechanism, ask whether comparable evidence exists outside the submarine anecdote -- for instance, the research on self-determination theory, cognitive dissonance, or high-reliability organizations covered in earlier lessons in this book, which stand on independent empirical footing regardless of how the submarine story is told. Mechanisms with that kind of independent support (curiosity over praise, qualification loops, pithy principles) deserve more confidence than mechanisms resting solely on narrative appeal. Adopting Leader-Leader well means separating the durable psychological substance from the specific, unrepeatable, dramatically satisfying story it arrived in.",
